    "Selected complete C3 lifecycle provides an early real producer/version/condition-bound fact attachment and invalidation operation over actual immutable syntax and actual change events. Later consume actual lexical bindings, serialized type solutions, effect records/graphs, applicable profile/ownership/safety facts and proof obligations from their owners. Preserve unaffected facts only when their conditions hold, invalidate affected facts before reuse and require actual owner regeneration where needed. Tentative/declared source data is distinct from later validated or inferred facts and actual grants. Only facts attached to the selected subject require their applicable producer products; read-phase construction does not wait for every semantic pass. Pipeline owns cross-stage preservation, semantic stages own computation, and Syntax owns this carrier lifecycle. Fixed demo ledgers, current flags or the example version=1 prove none of these operations.",
