rbidden labels, handler forms and modes before combined handler legality. Runtime execution, final Effects5 conformance and conditional new stable adoption are not prerequisites for checking existing source/profile contracts. A fixture interpreter never supplies an ambient permissive profile. Additional L11/SAFE8 profile compatibility consumes early actual hardware-clocked or GPU kernel/host-boundary definitions when those profiles are selected, alongside real provider/runtime support. Distinguish all thirteen source families and nine explicit L11 profile cases, refusing unsupported scheduling, blocking, shared mutation or target primitives. Source definitions precede their later emitted/device/simulation outcomes; final domain/backend conformance is no profile-check start gate. Physical executor/target limits survive project-accounting removal without input/work quotas or hidden host threads. Additional provider compatibility checks complete declared contracts/effects/targets/trust/isolation and revocation or permitted static-lifetime substitutes against the actual profile before final selection. Early declaration/support products precede this verdict; runtime initialization and owner conformance follow it. Ambient permission is explicit, untrusted isolation must actually exist, and no trusted signature or runtime fallback repairs compiler illegality. Additional L12 profile checker consumes early P requests and actual Q source declarations with fixed target/provider/isolation contracts, then supplies the actual profile verdict before affected evaluation or generated admission. Preserve all nine explicit cases: pure portable core, auditable granted hosted services, declared native targets, mandatory hermetic kernel/firmware/hardware with unmodeled-facility refusal, distributed workflow records, AI identity/retention/review and checked meta IR. Early definitions precede their own later conformance; no host fallback repairs a rejected profile. Additional joint macro profile boundary checks actual selected-provider support and early declared output constraints, then ordinary Q legality under its caller profile. Preserve same-macro hosted acceptance versus kernel reflection/core filesystem/illegal unsafe refusal; :safe is a safety mode, not a new profile. Explicit profile splits remain in provider declarations and artifacts; no host fallback repairs a rejected profile. Additional complete C3 profile boundary distinguishes early declared caller profile/phase context from the actual later profile verdict. Consume actual verified source/generated carrier and applicable current facts; require explicit producing-contract permission for a profile transition. Reject stale context or generated caller-profile bypass before downstream admission without turning a declared profile into proof. Additional complete L3/C5 profile result validates actual namespace clauses, one active implementation profile with the explicit seed exception, reusable variants/exclusions and requested targets without union powers. Early header/requested-import facts precede this checker; its actual admitted/refused boundary decision feeds the later checked graph. Check all five cross-profile boundary kinds with their concrete effect/authority/memory/safety evidence, reject artifact-hidden richer source and keep runtime availability from legalizing source. Resolve remains the graph recorder, not another profile checker. Complete L2/C6 profile checking uses the actual candidate/typed shape, effect projections and declared runtime/target support. Enforce core portability, var/redefinition/dispatch/heap-closure/exception constraints and caller-profile checking of generated code; hosted nulls/exceptions are normalized and constrained operations lower explicitly or reject. Candidate Core precedes checking and exported checked Core follows it. Preserve independently meaningful allocation/layout/ownership/target conditions without restoring work/input quotas.",
