e/homogeneous/private-entry/branch/loop premise, typed outcome/dispatch/schema/conversion/profile and latent-effect behavior. Cover both accepted and rejected empty, non-invoking, incomplete, circular, wrong-path, illegal and stale/substituted cases. Owner construction precedes independently executed harnesses; real runtime observations are required only for the selected claimed behavior and actual holds remain. Complete L7 independent language harness consumes actual owner family/profile fixtures and checked/runtime/representative-target products. Cover structural failure, once-only guards, true/false/non-Boolean/unknown/non-returning behavior, defaults/required coverage, unvalidated shapes, scoped bindings and linear paths. Owner preparation precedes independent execution; unavailable targets and held operations remain visible, and a source witness or structural projection is not language acceptance. Complete L8 independent language conformance consumes actual owner definitions/extensions/mode/effect/profile/host/tool/artifact fixtures and selected runtime/target results, including required optimizer-specialization fixtures for complete L8 acceptance. Valid unspecialized programs can compile earlier. Prepare fixtures before final harness execution; missing required mode/interface coverage or unavailable/held execution remains open. Equal result or container complete status does not establish the full source conjunction.",
