    "C9-selected source consumption/destination cleanup transfers, constructed and fact-annotated MIR, actual verification/admission, selected post-mutation preservation/regeneration, target/emitted behavior, actual runtime transfer/check/cleanup/failure and owning diagnostic/context results. Analysis products precede MIR construction; this task's final boundary evidence consumes the downstream results. Valid unoptimized MIR remains legal before Opt; these are task integration evidence requirements, not per-program legality or whole-component start gates. Held target/runtime/callback operations stay unassessed rather than substituted with supplied success flags. Additional C10-selected products are exact-condition/dominating proof or residual-check protection, Lower/backend assumption and source preservation, actually checked certificates and invalidation decisions, authenticated artifact trust, real capability enforcement hooks, distributed/AI provider check/failure/review/replay boundaries, emitted-byte/check/proof identity and applicable AI/workflow policy preservation results. Classification and facts precede construction; actual changed-function optimization checks, target/provider execution and boundary refusals are final composition evidence when those mechanisms are claimed. This consumer does not implement or grant those producer operations, require optimized MIR for a valid unoptimized program, or infer universal proof authority from one method. Additional SAFE1/SAFE6-selected composition consumes current-package P safety/unsafe summary and provenance validation, actual language-server safety views and generated API/audit documentation, plus distinct specialist audit revalidation/refusal when source/profile/backend/target/optimizer/wrapper assumptions change. Compiler classification first supplies P's local records; Build/Tools consume those exact records afterward, without requiring actual signing or publication to construct local checks. Imported Q trust inputs stay separate. Consumers preserve permitted/internal-only versus safe-export eligibility, every island and dependency summary, exact source identities and stale/expired/wrong-scope refusals. Actual external review, signing and publication retain their authority; this route grants none. Additional SAFE2-SAFE5 final composition consumes actual C14 ABI/layout and target-matched provider decisions, Backend verified-input/proof-target/emitted-memory metadata results, and Runtime linked/loaded service agreement in addition to existing real memory/startup/check/cleanup/transfer results. Reconcile derived layout, field/range/padding/packing/ABI/address-space and provider identities with the earlier typed analysis and every surviving proof/check assumption; changed layouts or providers require valid preservation or invalidation/reanalysis and a retained legal check or refusal. Lowering cannot legalize an earlier rejection or attach noalias/dereferenceable/alignment from a declaration. Demonstrate checks before access, initialized-only drop, at-most-once region cleanup and exactly-once linear cleanup/transfer across every modeled exit under declared failure/unwind/cancellation policy. Preserve region/generation/reset and concurrent/foreign/device transfer facts, source/generated/debug origins and actual diagnostic identities. These are final selected-boundary results after legal analysis and verified MIR, never whole Lower/Backend/Runtime completion or a new allocation/execution gate before local analysis. Additional L10/L18 preservation consumes actual checked allocation/memory/volatile/MMIO/atomic/barrier ordering from its Effects owner along with the existing MIR/Opt/Lower/Runtime products. Reconcile provider/layout/source and proof assumptions at actual allocation/release/transfer/check boundaries; invalidate/recheck changed facts and retain a legal check or refuse. Actual public library consumers feed family conformance later, rather than becoming a prerequisite for the service that they call. Additional complete concurrency handoff has early and later products. Export actual checked source-derived task/scope/capture/move/sync/atomic/schema/replay/check/unsafe obligations before MIR and target consumers. Later consume actual verified MIR, affected Opt/Lower preservation, selected GPU/HDL artifacts, Runtime/library execution and enforcement traces for the claimed end-to-end result; these later results cannot be prerequisites for their own input facts. Preserve source sequential-consistency defaults unless an explicit governing profile/library permits weaker order, target scope/fence/alignment support and affected invalidation. Record copying or a supplied safe flag is not preservation evidence. Additional provider preservation exports actual checked effect/capability/provider/grant/phase/scope/lifetime/trust/isolation obligations before MIR and target use, then consumes exact installed-gate, startup, build/runtime and invalidation results for the claimed end-to-end case. Bind actual artifacts to source/compiler/profile/target/policy identities, invalidate changed assumptions, and preserve redacted diagnostics and audit records. Later execution and cache reuse cannot supply earlier legality or authority; imported Q inputs remain distinct from P's later output evidence. Additional joint macro downstream preservation consumes actual ordinary Q decisions and syntax-origin/safety/taint/unsafe/authority products, then retains them into MIR, selected lowering and runtime artifacts. Reject lost capture/SAFE6/sink/profile obligations or forged generated-safe labels. This is actual preservation/composition, not reimplementation of macro execution or a new full-runtime construction gate. Additional complete C3 checked handoff retains actual source/generated maps, hygiene, producer/version/invalidation and ordinary profile/safety facts through syntax-derived Core/MIR interfaces. Require actual owner replacement/regeneration or surviving checks where preservation fails. C3 verification and metadata cannot replace later MIR/runtime semantic enforcement or establish seed retirement. Complete L5/C7 safety handoff preserves actual current resource/layout/schema/dynamic/conversion facts, their proof/check/reject/unsafe verdicts and complete invalidation into MIR and selected runtime metadata. Every consuming stage reconstructs required private-entry/key-domain/loop premises rather than trusting an earlier solved flag. Required checks and failure semantics survive actual later lowering/execution; their declared records are not execution evidence. Complete L7 handoff preserves real checked pattern control, validation/check obligations, move/borrow/linear and effect/order/replay facts into current MIR and selected runtime products. Bind every table and source/generated origin to the same subject, invalidate changed premises and reject lost obligations. A decision skeleton or evaluation label is not actual analysis or installed enforcement.",
