hese cases. Owner results are not independent Release suite runs, broad target availability or current independent acceptance; held cases remain unassessed. Additional complete L3/C5 legality conformance produces its own actual accepted/refused namespace/profile/graph/checker fixtures and consumer-preservation products from the selected resolver outputs. Cover missing/multiple profiles, the explicit seed exception, library exclusions, all five cross-profile boundaries, unavailable effects/grants and illegal initialization. These owner cases precede the independent language/compiler/profile harnesses that consume them; completion of those later full suites cannot be the owner fixtures' first construction input. Preserve the exact candidate, source/diagnostic and existing independent acceptance scope without promoting the narrow historical SH06 receipt. Complete L2/C6 owner conformance uses actual primitive/handwritten/generated and profile/guard/error/order/refusal cases through Core, real semantic checkers and selected MIR/transform/target/runtime consumers. Early owner fixture preparation and candidate checks precede the independently executed release harnesses. Require actual selected execution only for the claimed cases, not completed every-target/library acceptance before constructing Core. Preserve all artifacts/diagnostics, finite historical scopes and every held operation. Complete L5/C7 owner conformance covers every type family and complete independent inference premise, actual schema/protocol/generic/layout products, profile-specific Dynamic and annotations, checked/unsafe conversions, latent effects and verifier refusals. Include empty/normal versus Never/non-invoking entries, private visibility/use/escape/mutation/re-entry gaps, wrong value/path refinements, circular cold grounding, stale/substituted complete artifacts and actual typed-to-MIR preservation. Prepare owner fixtures before independent harnesses; no final suite or held execution becomes an or