    "Selected L15/SAFE10 cache owner consumes authentic selected source/project/lock/compiler/pass/profile/target/provider/version/grant/policy and recorded build-input identities plus actual stage/action outputs. Construct the real key/entry/dependency graph, detect changed provider/scope/policy/replay assumptions and perform required invalidation/revalidation before reuse. Keep secret values out of stable public keys, generated code, diagnostics and artifacts; a digest-only policy label is not proof of redaction. This task owns shared/default cache construction and completeness/current-policy admission/invalidation/revalidation integration, accepting authentic permitted L16 engine-specific key/entry/trace/replay results; repeat-build comparison consumes its results later. A successful prior action or content hash alone cannot validate stale evidence or mint authority for a new one. Additional complete L12 cache producer consumes actual stage/value/trace products and all semantic input identities, including function/extension versions, source spans, facets and current grant/replay/target policy. Construct keys/entries and revalidate before reuse; actual Expand4 use/refusal traces arrive later for clean-versus-reused comparison. Do not wait for a hit's own future result to produce its initial cache decision. Preserve stricter-policy invalidation, hidden-effect refusal after relaxation, secret-safe environment digests/presence and target representation. Pipeline supplies stage facts and consumes decisions; it does not create a second cache authority. Additional joint macro shared cache integrates actual selected-engine keys/entries/trace/replay/current-policy products under complete semantic-input admission/invalidation/revalidation. Engine-specific storage and scheduling remain permitted. Actual stage/definition/provider facts precede decisions; actual later hit/refusal/use and clean-versus-reused artifacts/diagnostics verify them. Stricter-policy mismatch, hidden creation effects after relaxation, incomplete inputs and secret leakage refuse reuse. Pipeline integrates facts/results without duplicating machinery. Additional complete C3 cache result uses actual semantic syntax identities, complete selected serialized subjects and real producer-conditioned invalidation/currentness decisions before a hit or dependent artifact use. Apply stage-specific owner and current-policy revalidation; reject stale syntax, facts, origin diagnostics or proofs rather than trusting timestamps, hashes alone or current flags. Preserve permitted engine-specific machinery under shared Build policy. No repeated external action authorizes a cache hit, and source-only cache subjects do not require later semantic products they do not contain. Additional complete L3/C5 cache reuse consumes actual semantic binding/module identities and producer-owned affected invalidation/recheck decisions for all nine resolution causes. Only facts present in the selected cache subject require their actual owner products; source-only caches do not wait for later type or checked-module facts they do not contain. Semantic-id stability under docs/formatting does not permit stale physical origins, diagnostics, public API or policy. Preserve permitted engine machinery and actual current-policy admission; hashes or current flags alone are insufficient. Complete L2/C6 cache reuse binds actual source/desugaring rule/graph/schema/profile/semantic-policy inputs and producer-owned invalidation to the selected cache stage. Early syntax/Core-only entries do not await later analyses or execution absent from their subject; typed/MIR/optimized entries require the actual included facts and current affected rechecks. Reject stale rule, source/generated diagnostics, node/table/anchor or proof assumptions; equivalent values or stable semantic ids cannot authorize stale provenance.",
