    "Selected L6 authority consumes actual typed source/phase/principal requirements, early direct/latent inferred action sets, profile compatibility, validated compatible provider declarations, normalized package/build/deployment configuration and runtime support descriptors. Map effect requirements to separately checked capability grants; never compare effect sets directly with capability sets or copy allowances as inference. Early inferred requirements precede grant-dependent final handler legality. Bind live/mock/fixture/replay-read/write/scheduler/tool scope, lifetime and provider, refuse ambient/widened authority, and preserve missing-capability tests as expected diagnostics rather than hidden grants. Runtime support metadata does not execute an action or manufacture authority. Additional concurrency authority binds actual scheduler/atomic/lock/channel/actor/provider requests to separate inferred effects, source/profile/principal/deployment and lifetime/revocation facts. Runtime5 supplies early actual sink/gate capability interfaces before action use; later actual denial/revocation/narrowing traces are evidence of enforcement, not prior grants. Neither runtime model selection, a message schema nor an unsafe label supplies authority or policy-required review; preserve allowed audit-only records without a new ordinary-development gate. Additional L15/SAFE10 grant derivation consumes actual source/namespace and function type/effect requirements, package and dependency requests/denials, workspace/profile, build/deployment invocation and provider scopes. Normalize requests first, then compute the actual eight-layer non-expanding intersection and category-specific operation scopes. Types preserve provider/scope/phase/lifetime/thread-safety/revocation; pure transport grants no later action. Required imported trust verification precedes provider use but never supplies authority. Preserve explicit ambient premises, attenuation, supported revocation/static lifetimes, secret read/export policy and actual failure/redaction decisions; supplied scope or safe flags do not prove them. Additional L12 grant/secret interface consumes real P source/function/namespace identity and actual requested effect/principal/provider/scope/phase facts. Early typed requests and destination/redaction contracts precede grant derivation and action; later evaluator/cache/plugin/diagnostic results witness secret-safe handling and denial. Requests, signed lockfiles, local profiles and provider configuration do not mint wider authority. Public code/diagnostics/keys/provenance exclude secrets; explicitly accepting private storage retains its own held policy boundary. Preserve actual external billing without project cost/fuel or mandatory replacement proof gates. Additional complete L3/C5 grant result consumes actual namespace/import capability requirements and package/build/deployment identities, then checks the real applicable grant intersection separately from effect allowance. Resolve supplies declared requested edges before validation and consumes the later verdict before checked use; no capability name or public module record issues authority. Reject unavailable or widened grants with real action-independent decisions, preserving held operations and seed/profile distinctions.",
